<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bengal</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bengal is a region in the northeast of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-subcontinent">Indian subcontinent</a>, centred on the delta of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ganges-plain">Ganges</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brahmaputra">Brahmaputra</a> rivers, and long one of its richest agricultural and commercial areas. It broke away from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi-sultanate">Delhi Sultanate</a> in 1339 and was never recovered by later sultans. In the eighteenth century Bengal was a target of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha</a> raids, and its conquest by the British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-india-company">East India Company</a> provided the base for British expansion in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bengal.jpg" alt="Bengal" width="320" height="307" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bengal_in_Asia.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
